    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate on 2026-09-21, the Austin Waves offense centers around the elite production profile of **Gunnar Henderson**. With a robust score of 81.88, **Gunnar Henderson** holds the highest efficiency rating in the lineup, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Yesavage. The combination of hitting third in the order and the significant park factors currently in play makes him our primary anchor. Similarly, **Coby Mayo** earns a Strong rating of 61.78; while he faces a slight platoon disadvantage against the right-handed Yesavage, his current recency trend and high-value spot in the fourth hole provide enough leverage to keep him firmly in the starting rotation.\n\nThe most difficult roster construction decision involved managing the marginal threshold for our utility spots, particularly regarding **Heliot Ramos** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** While both were analyzed extensively, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** just missed the starting cut due to his reliance on stolen base volume, which currently carries high risk against a catcher-pitcher battery favoring runners today. We are playing it conservative with our game caps, opting to leave **Heliot Ramos** on the bench despite his contact profile, as the park factors do not align well enough to push him above our 60-point \"Strong\" threshold. We remain cautious regarding **Luis Robert Jr.**, who continues to be held in the IL slot, while **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** are effectively inactive today due to team off-days. With **Drake Baldwin**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Andy Pages** providing depth, we are positioned to navigate the late-season volatility while preserving our remaining daily game limits.",
